# Proposed aisle for every distinct name extracted from the Things "Groceries"
# project (issue #121, epic #135). One offline pass — there is no runtime AI in
# this app, by design.
#
# Format: name|section|confidence|notes        (`#` starts a comment line)
#
# The key is the name LOWERCASED, matching `catalog_items`' unique index on
# (household_id, lower(name)). Names are kept VERBATIM — whitespace and case
# normalization only. Compound names are NOT split: "Soy Sauces: Light, Dark
# Sweet, and Dark" is a slightly long staple, which beats a mangled one.
#
# Confidence drives the review order in the Google Sheet: `low` first, so the
# genuinely ambiguous dozen are read first and the obvious 500 are below them.
# `notes` carries anything Jon should see — near-duplicates, quantities baked
# into a name, and items that probably shouldn't be staples at all.
